    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nall of the above\n\n### Question\n\nI'm very new to using the mini ecosystem. I used the example init.lua template for mini.deps to get started. https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/scripts/init-deps-example.lua. It's been working well so far and I have made a few modifications but for some reason I can't see any of the mini help tags when I use the builtin search. As in, if I do `:h MiniPick` it says \"E149: Sorry, no help for MiniPick\" but I can do `:Pick files` and it works as expected. I tried using `:Pick help` to see if maybe the list would be different but again no luck.\r\n\r\nI can always go and read the help file on github but it would be nice if I could read it directly in neovim.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">all of the above</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm very new to using the mini ecosystem. I used the example init.lua template for mini.deps to get started. <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/scripts/init-deps-example.lua\">https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/scripts/init-deps-example.lua</a>. It's been working well so far and I have made a few modifications but for some reason I can't see any of the mini help tags when I use the builtin search. As in, if I do <code class=\"notranslate\">:h MiniPick</code> it says \"E149: Sorry, no help for MiniPick\" but I can do <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick files</code> and it works as expected. I tried using <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick help</code> to see if maybe the list would be different but again no luck.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I can always go and read the help file on github but it would be nice if I could read it directly in neovim.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nall of the above\nQuestion\nI'm very new to using the mini ecosystem. I used the example init.lua template for mini.deps to get started. https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/scripts/init-deps-example.lua. It's been working well so far and I have made a few modifications but for some reason I can't see any of the mini help tags when I use the builtin search. As in, if I do :h MiniPick it says \"E149: Sorry, no help for MiniPick\" but I can do :Pick files and it works as expected. I tried using :Pick help to see if maybe the list would be different but again no luck.\nI can always go and read the help file on github but it would be nice if I could read it directly in neovim.",
